 Messages exist in English (`en`) and Korean (`ko`), in
 `src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+
+## POST /import/sales
+
+Send a JSON object with a `csv` string containing the columns
+`ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty`. Each row records a positive whole number of
+portions of the dish. `soldAt` is an ISO instant with a time zone.
+The response contains `tickets` (distinct new tickets) and `dishes` (total
+portions imported). A new ticket can have multiple rows. Tickets recorded
+by a previous import are skipped. Invalid rows and insufficient stock
+reject the whole file, and the error identifies the CSV row.
+
+## GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD
+
+Returns rows ordered by `itemId`, with `theoretical`, `actual`, and
+`variance` (actual minus theoretical) in the item's unit. Both dates are
+inclusive UTC days. Theoretical use comes from the recipes recorded for
+sales in that range. Actual use sums all consume movements in the range.
+Items appear when either quantity is positive.
